ttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3116#issuecomment-533426587"},"message":"While looking into https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3637 and a possible fix https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/3688 I realized that this bug is potentially pointing at the same underlying issue: https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/3688#issuecomment-533090988","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1569068945,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDUzMzc5NDI5NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3116#issuecomment-533794295"},"message":"OK, here is the state of things on win10 with current master:\n\n```\n(base) C:\\Users\\mih\u003edatalad create quote\n[INFO] Creating a new annex repo at C:\\Users\\mih\\quote\n[INFO]   Detected a filesystem without fifo support.\n[INFO]   Disabling ssh connection caching.\n[INFO]   Detected a crippled filesystem.\n[INFO]   Entering an adjusted branch where files are unlocked as this filesystem does not support locked files.\n[INFO] Switched to branch 'adjusted/master(unlocked)'\ncreate(ok): C:\\Users\\mih\\quote (dataset)\n\n(base) C:\\Users\\mih\u003ecd quote\n\n(base) C:\\Users\\mih\\quote\u003edatalad run cp .gitattributes test\n[INFO] == Command start (output follows) =====\n[INFO] == Command exit (modification check follows) =====\nadd(ok): test (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n\n(base) C:\\Users\\mih\\quote\u003egit log\ncommit c0d16c97feddbf263d5b69be086022ca425ef95f\nAuthor: Michael Hanke \u003cmichael.hanke@gmail.com\u003e\nDate:   Sat Sep 21 13:56:53 2019 +0200\n\n    [DATALAD RUNCMD] cp .gitattributes test\n\n    === Do not change lines below ===\n    {\n     \"chain\": [],\n     \"cmd\": \"cp .gitattributes test\",\n     \"dsid\": \"d41d2764-dc66-11e9-8e06-309c23c2cf5c\",\n     \"exit\": 0,\n     \"extra_inputs\": [],\n     \"inputs\": [],\n     \"outputs\": [],\n     \"pwd\": \".\"\n    }\n    ^^^ Do not change lines above ^^^\n```\n\nSo there is no fundamental issue with `datalad run`.\n\nNow for the full replication:\n\n```\n(base) C:\\Users\\mih\\quote\u003egit annex addurl https://nifti.nimh.nih.gov/nifti-1/data/avg152T1_LR_nifti.nii.gz\naddurl https://nifti.nimh.nih.gov/nifti-1/data/avg152T1_LR_nifti.nii.gz\n(to nifti.nimh.nih.gov_nifti_1_data_avg152T1_LR_nifti.nii.gz) ok\n(recording state in git...)\n\n(base) C:\\Users\\mih\\quote\u003edatalad save\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\n\n(base) C:\\Users\\mih\\quote\u003enib-ls -s nifti.nimh.nih.gov_nifti_1_data_avg152T1_LR_nifti.nii.gz\nnifti.nimh.nih.gov_nifti_1_data_avg152T1_LR_nifti.nii.gz uint8 [ 91, 109,  91] 2.00x2.00x2.00   sform [902569] [1, 2.6e+02]\n\n(base) C:\\Users\\mih\\quote\u003edatalad run 'nib-ls -s nifti.nimh.nih.gov_nifti_1_data_avg152T1_LR_nifti.nii.gz \u003e INFO.txt'\n\n(base) C:\\Users\\mih\\quote\u003els\n\"INFO.txt'\"   nifti.nimh.nih.gov_nifti_1_data_avg152T1_LR_nifti.nii.gz   test\n```\n\nClearly, the command line handling is broken, because the filename ends up being `INFO.txt'`. For reasons unclear to me `datalad run` also does not pick up the created file.\n\n```\n(base) C:\\Users\\mih\\quote\u003edatalad status OR datalad diff\nuntracked: INFO.txt' (file)\n```\n\nHowever, switching to double-quotes let's datalad behave as desired:\n\n```\n(base) C:\\Users\\mih\\quote\u003edatalad run \"nib-ls -s nifti.nimh.nih.gov_nifti_1_data_avg152T1_LR_nifti.nii.gz \u003e INFO.txt\"\n[INFO] == Command start (output follows) =====\n[INFO] == Command exit (modification check follows) =====\nadd(ok): INFO.txt (file)\nsave(ok): . (dataset)\naction summary:\n  add (ok: 1)\n  save (ok: 1)\n\n(base) C:\\Users\\mih\\quote\u003egit log\ncommit 88a66ac1b87c22528634bbd54fdd095c154a0871 (HEAD -\u003e adjusted/master(unlocked))\nAuthor: Michael Hanke \u003cmichael.hanke@gmail.com\u003e\nDate:   Sat Sep 21 14:14:03 2019 +0200\n\n    [DATALAD RUNCMD] nib-ls -s nifti.nimh.nih.gov_nifti_1_dat...\n\n    === Do not change lines below ===\n    {\n     \"chain\": [],\n     \"cmd\": \"nib-ls -s nifti.nimh.nih.gov_nifti_1_data_avg152T1_LR_nifti.nii.gz \u003e INFO.txt\",\n     \"dsid\": \"d41d2764-dc66-11e9-8e06-309c23c2cf5c\",\n     \"exit\": 0,\n     \"extra_inputs\": [],\n     \"inputs\": [],\n     \"outputs\": [],\n     \"pwd\": \".\"\n    }\n    ^^^ Do not change lines above ^^^\n```\n\nBased on this result I conclude that\n\n1) I have little to no idea on how quoting is supposed to work on Windows (or more specifically with `subprocess` on Windows)\n2) we can close the bug, because the original behavior can no longer be found. But we have to take care of https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3697","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1569068945,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50MjY1MjA5ODcwNg=="},"status":2}]}